  "text": "CONTRADICTING: At 25-26 DIV, ApoE4 neurons had 19.8% fewer LysoTracker-positive vesicles per cell body than ApoE3 neurons (normalized means 0.303 vs 0.370). This indicates fewer acidic compartments with ApoE4 rather than increased acidification.",
  "description": "Same as Fig 4J: APOE3 and APOE4 targeted-replacement mouse primary hippocampal/cortical mixed cultures at 25-26 DIV, synapsin-GFP-labelled neurons, live LysoTracker Red imaging on Operetta CLS. Analysed by one-way ANOVA with post hoc Tukey; N = embryos, 6-10 fields per N. Caveat: mouse neurons, not human astrocytes; aged cultures; vesicle count of acidic compartments is a weak surrogate for endosomal pH.",
